       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID.     SR3REQEX.
      *REMARKS.
      *D    THIS SUBPROGRAM PROCESSES THE REQUISITIONS THAT HAD THE
      *D    FINAL APPROVER SIGNOFF ON A CSIS REQUISITION. THE
      *D    REQUISITION NUMBER WAS STORED IN MCORPREQ WITH AN 'R3'
      *D    STATUS. A FILE IS CONSTRUCTED FROM THIS SAVED DATA AND
      *D    PASSED TO THE MAINFRAME FOR SAP/R3 TO UPLOAD INTO ITS
      *D    FILES. THIS LOGIC IS FOR MEDICINE HAT ONLY FOR NOW AS
      *D    THEY WILL BE THE ONLY SAP/R3 PLANT THROUGH THE YEAR 2000.
      *D
      *D    18FEB2002 - DAVE PLUM
      *D    REVISED TO:
      *D     1) ZERO FILL THE 4TH BYTE OF REQ-SUBD (DEPT) IF IT IS
      *D        BLANK.  (FREEPORT ONLY USES 3 DIGIT DEPARTMENT NUMBERS.)
      *D     2) ZERO FILL THE FINAL 5 BYTES OF THE SAP-ACCT-NO-I1 FIELD.
      *D        BYTES 2 THROUGH 6 OF THE REQ-A-D-6 FIELD (ADDITIONAL
      *D        DATA) HAD BEEN PLACED IN THESE FINAL 5 BYTES OF THE
      *D        SAP ACCOUNT NUMBER FIELD.  (WE HAD BEEN TRYING TO FIT
      *D        19 BYTES OF DATA INTO A 18 BYTE FIELD BY DROPPING THE
      *D        FIRST BYTE OF THE EXPENSE CLASS/NEW WORK/ADDITIONAL DATA
      *D        FIELD.
      *D     3) ADDED A NEW FIELD (SAP-INTERNAL-ORDER) TO THE
      *D        R3-RECORD-T1 RECORD WHICH WILL BE POPULATED WHEN THE
      *D        REQ-A-D-6 (ADDITONAL DATA) FIELD CONTAINS A 6 DIGIT
      *D        NUMBER.  THIS SIX DIGIT NUMBER WILL BE AN SAP
      *D        INTERNAL ORDER NUMBER IN AN R/3 PLANT.
      *D     4) IF AN SAP INTERNAL ORDER NUMBER IS FOUND, THE
      *D        SAP-ACCT-CAT-I1 FIELD WILL BE SET TO "F" INSTEAD OF "K".
      *D
      *C    02/20/2002   CA YODER
      *C        CHANGED THE NOTIFY FIELD ON THE HEADER FROM THE DOCK
      *C        NOTIFY USER-ID TO THE CLOCK CARD NUMBER.  ALSO ADDED
      *C        THE DOCK NOTIFY USER-ID TO THE I1 RECORD.
      *C
      *C    03/01/2002   DAVE PLUM
      *C        REARRANGED THE FIELDS FOLLOWING THE 18 BYTE ACCOUNTING
      *C        DATA SECTION OF THE I1 RECORD ACCORDING TO R/3
      *C        REQUIREMENTS.  ALSO STOPPED PASSING THE MMIS WORK ORDER
      *C        NUMBER.
      *C
      *C    04/25/2002   CA YODER
      *C        FOR SAP INTERNAL ORDER NUMBER, MOVE REQ-ADDL-INFO FIELD
      *C        INSTEAD OF ADDITIONAL DATA FIELD.  ALSO, MOVE LAST 3
      *C        BYTES OF REQ ADDITIONAL DATA FIELD (EXPENSE CLASS)
      *C        TO CLASS FIELD (SAP-ACCT-SUB-I1).
      *C
      *C    07/09/2002   CA YODER      J. THOMAS REQUEST
      *C        INSTEAD OF PASSING THE DOCK NOTIFY USER-ID ON THE I1
      *C        RECORD, SEND THE REQ ORIGINATOR NAME.  IF NO CLOCK
      *C        CARD NUMBER EXISTS FOR THE REQ, SEND THE LITERAL
      *C        "STOREROOM".
      *C
      *C    07/30/2002   CA YODER
      *C        IF THE REQ HAS A TAX CODE SPECIFIED, SEND THE TAX
      *C        CODE AND DESCRIPTION IN AN "I4" REMARKS RECORD.
      *C
      *C    11/21/2002   CA YODER
      *C        FIXED PROBLEM WITH REQS HAVING > 12 LINES OF DESCRIPTION.
      *C        THE DESCRIPTION WAS NEVER WRITTEN TO THE FILE IF THIS
      *C        CONDITION EXISTED.
      *C
      *C    04/21/2003   BRUCE GEISER
      *C        DETERMINE REQ TYPE BY CHECKING NEW REQ-SERVICE-FLAG.
      *C
      *C    08/13/2003   BRUCE GEISER
      *C        FIXED PROBLEM WITH REQS HAVING > 12 LINES OF DESCRIPTION.
      *C        THE LOGIC THAT WAS DETERMINING WHERE TO SPLIT THE LINE
      *C        WAS GOING OVER THE TABLE LIMIT. ALSO ADDED LOGIC FOR
      *C        REPAIR AND RETURN REQS TO CREATE "RR" TYPE SAP DOCUMENTS.
      *C
      *C    10/06/2004   DAN RAUCH    DCR01  REQUEST# 2004-50231
      *C        FIXED PROBLEM WHERE PROGRAM ABENDS WHEN THERE ARE NO   N.
      *C        BLANKS IN THE 40 CHARACTER DESCRIPTION. MOVE ALL 40
      *C        CHARACTERS INSTEAD OF TRYING TO SPLIT THE DESC FIELD.
      *C***************************************************************


       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       CONFIGURATION SECTION.

       SOURCE-COMPUTER.          IBM-AS400.
       OBJECT-COMPUTER.          IBM-AS400.

       COPY SPECIALN IN COPYLIB.
       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
       FILE-CONTROL.

           SELECT DREQD
               ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS2101
               ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
               ACCESS IS DYNAMIC
               RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
               FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT DREQDESC
               ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS2301
               ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
               ACCESS IS DYNAMIC
               RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
               WITH DUPLICATES
               FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT DREQITM
               ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS2201
               ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
               ACCESS IS DYNAMIC
               RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
               FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT DCOMMENT
               ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS1901
               ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
               ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
               RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
               WITH DUPLICATES
               FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT MPLTINFO
               ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS0501
               ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
               ACCESS IS DYNAMIC
               RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
               FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT MREQ
               ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS2001
               ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
               ACCESS IS DYNAMIC
               RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
               FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT REQUISITION-FILE
               ASSIGN TO DATABASE-R3REQDATA
               ORGANIZATION IS SEQUENTIAL
               ACCESS IS SEQUENTIAL
               FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT PERS-FILE
               ASSIGN       TO DATABASE-MCFLMM0301
               ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
               ACCESS MODE  IS DYNAMIC
               RECORD KEY   IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
               FILE STATUS  IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT R3FILE     ASSIGN TO DISK-R3REQFI2.


           SELECT R3-REQ-RPT ASSIGN TO DISK-R3REQRPT.


       DATA DIVISION.
       FILE SECTION.
       FD  DREQD
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD
           DATA RECORD IS DREQD-REC.
       01  DREQD-REC.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS2100  OF MCFLCS2101.

       FD  DREQDESC
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD
           DATA RECORD IS DREQDESC-REC.
       01  DREQDESC-REC.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS2300  OF MCFLCS2301.

       FD  DREQITM
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD
           DATA RECORD IS DREQITM-REC.
       01  DREQITM-REC.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS2200  OF MCFLCS2201.

       FD  DCOMMENT
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  DCOMMENT-REC.
           COPY DDS-ALL-FORMATS OF MCFLCS1901.

       FD  MPLTINFO
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD
           DATA RECORD IS MPLTINFO-REC.
       01  MPLTINFO-REC.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS0500  OF MCFLCS0501.

       FD  MREQ
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD
           DATA RECORD IS MREQ-REC.
       01  MREQ-REC.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS2000  OF MCFLCS2001.

       FD  PERS-FILE
           LABEL RECORDS       ARE STANDARD.
       01  PERS-REC.
           COPY DDS-ALL-FORMATS OF MCFLMM0301.

       FD  REQUISITION-FILE
           DATA RECORD IS REQ-REC.
       01  REQ-REC                PIC X(200).

       FD  R3FILE
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  R3FILE-REC.
           05  R3FILE-REQNO       PIC X(12).
           05  FILLER             PIC X(8).

       FD  R3-REQ-RPT
           LABEL RECORDS ARE OMITTED
           RECORD CONTAINS 133 CHARACTERS
           DATA RECORD IS R3-PRINT-RCD.
       01  R3-PRINT-RCD.
           05  R3-PRINT-CTL       PIC 9.
           05  R3-PRINT-LINE      PIC X(132).

       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       77  HOLD-PLT-ID            PIC X.
       77  HOLD-LEGACY-ID         PIC X(2).
       77  HOLD-TEXT              PIC X(72).
       77  HOLD-UNIT-PRICE        PIC 9(11)V9(4).
       77  HOLD-PLANT-CODE        PIC X(4).
       77  HOLD-HOME-CUR          PIC X(2).
       77  HOLD-DEPT-STR          PIC X(4).
       77  HOLD-SHORT-TEXT        PIC X(80).
       77  LINE-CTR               PIC 99.
       77  RECS-CTR               PIC 9(6).
